# KS-1123 - Wednesday's task for Ornith, VITEST, **TEST-ONLY MODE, ONE NEW TEST FILE** (written 16:35 AEST on 2026-09-17)

Written from origin develop `f8c7aaa39dabfe6a3916e5be55d9ccd752e7d8ed`, re-read by `git ls-remote` from a scratch clone. The
product file `Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/src/routes/verification.ts` (1479 lines) was read at `:240-:260`
(`confidenceForAnchorStatus`) and `:619-:750` (the persisted reads, `persistedAnchored` and the confidence decision of the tier-1
verify route). The reference test `ks1123-f3-empty-status-is-off-chain.test.ts` (169 lines, the test that drives the REAL verify
route through a stub originate server) was read whole. KS-1123 and its 3 comments were read. This brief is the residue the #1002
gate left open (F-1002-1). **PRE-MEASURED** in a scratch clone at the tip; see `## Premises (measured)`.

## THE MODE - read this twice

TEST-ONLY, ONE NEW FILE. Your diff contains EXACTLY ONE file: the NEW test file
`Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/src/__tests__/ks1123-api-gateway-verify-an-empty-string.test.ts`, written as
`--- /dev/null` then `+++ b/...`, one `@@ -0,0 +1,113 @@` hunk, every line `+`.
**Do NOT modify `routes/verification.ts`**, and do NOT modify `ks1123-f3-empty-status-is-off-chain.test.ts` (the reference test).
`verification.ts` is in files[...] only so you can see the route the new test drives. The checker plants the tamper named at the
bottom into a clone of `verification.ts` and expects the two red cells RED and the control GREEN, then expects every cell GREEN at
the untouched tip.

## What is wrong (one paragraph)

The tier-1 verify route `POST /api/documents/:id/verify` reads the persisted anchor status at `:624` with a nullish default:
`(doc as any).blockchain?.status ?? null`. Because of the `??`, an empty-string, `0` or `false` status stays a status, it is not
`'confirmed'`, and the blob answers `verified: false` with `verificationConfidence: 'off-chain-only'`. If that read turned `0` or
`false` into `null`, the statusless carve-out at `:722` (`persistedStatus == null`) would fire and a blob with a real hash and
height would answer `on-chain` with `verified: true`. The merged file `ks1123-f3-empty-status-is-off-chain.test.ts` pins only the
empty-string status. The #1002 QA gate measured it: a read that keeps strings but drops `0` and `false` leaves the whole suite
green. **This task:** a NEW test file drives the real route with a `0` status and a `false` status, each with a real hash and
height, and asserts both answer `200, false, 'off-chain-only'`. No product line changes.

## Where (no product site changes - this list is informational; every line below STAYS)

- `:624` - (correct) `    const persistedStatus = (doc as any).blockchain?.status ?? null;` - the status read. The tamper replaces this line. Stays.
- `:722` - (correct) the `persistedAnchored` conjunct that accepts `'confirmed'` or a null status on tier 1. Stays.
- `:248` - (correct) `    case 'confirmed':` - the only status the confidence mapping calls on-chain. Stays.

## The test - CREATE THE NEW FILE `Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/src/__tests__/ks1123-api-gateway-verify-an-empty-string.test.ts`

**Harness:** `vitest run` inside `Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway`. To run this file alone:
`npx vitest run src/__tests__/ks1123-api-gateway-verify-an-empty-string.test.ts`.

The file does what the reference test does, trimmed to tier 1. A stub originate server on `127.0.0.1` port 0 answers
`GET /api/documents/doc-ks1123-falsy` with a document whose `blockchain` blob is whatever the cell sets. `globalThis.fetch` is
replaced so the live anchoring scan finds nothing, and the REAL `createVerificationRoutes` is mounted on an express app on
`127.0.0.1` port 0. `verify(blob)` posts to the verify route with the saved real fetch and answers the array
`[http status, verified, verificationConfidence]`. No database, no Redis, no off-host socket.

**Reproduce the body below EXACTLY as written.** It is 113 lines. Do not shorten it, do not replace any part with a comment, do
not invent a helper, do not rename a variable, do not collapse the cells into a loop or an `it.each`. Every name a cell reads
(`EXPECTED_CELLS`, `CELLS_RUN`, `REAL_TX`, `verify`) is declared ABOVE the first cell. **The file contains no backslash, no
template literal, no backtick, no dollar sign, no double quote and no non-ASCII character; keep it that way.** Every string is
single-quoted; URLs are built with `+`, not a template literal. The comments contain no quote character of any kind.

**Indentation, stated line by line (2 spaces per level, spaces only, no tabs):** the header comment lines ` * ...` start with ONE
space. Top-level `import`, `const`, `let`, `beforeAll(`, `afterAll(`, `async function` and `describe(` lines have no indent. Inside
`beforeAll`: each statement is indented 2 spaces (`originate = ...`, `originate.listen(...)`, `await new Promise...`,
`const originateUrl`, `globalThis.fetch = ...`, `const { createVerificationRoutes }`, `const mockBodyParser`, `const app`,
`app.use(`, `);`, `gateway = ...`, `gatewayPort = ...`); inside the `http.createServer` callback the statements are indented 4
spaces and the body of its `if` 6 spaces; `createVerificationRoutes({` is indented 4 spaces, its property lines 6 spaces, the lines
inside `authenticateToken` and `redisService` 8 spaces, and the `}),` closing it 4 spaces. Inside `afterAll` and inside `verify`
each statement is indented 2 spaces. Each `it(` line is indented 2 spaces; inside a cell every statement is indented 4 spaces; the
cell's closing `});` is indented 2 spaces. The final `});` closing `describe` has no indent.

```ts
/**
 * KS-1123 F-1002-1: the verify route reads the persisted anchor status with a
 * nullish default, so an empty-string, 0 or false status stays a status and a
 * blob carrying one answers off-chain-only. Only the empty-string case was
 * pinned. A read that keeps strings but turns 0 or false into null fires the
 * statusless carve-out, and those blobs answer on-chain with verified true.
 * These cells pin the 0 and false statuses on tier 1.
 */
import { describe, it, expect, beforeAll, afterAll, vi } from 'vitest';
import express from 'express';
import http from 'node:http';
import type { Server } from 'node:http';
import type { AddressInfo } from 'node:net';
import type { RequestHandler } from 'express';

const EXPECTED_CELLS = 3;
let CELLS_RUN = 0;
const REAL_TX = 'a'.repeat(64);
const DOC_ID = 'doc-ks1123-falsy';
const CONTENT_HASH = 'b'.repeat(64);
const realFetch = globalThis.fetch;

let gateway: Server;
let originate: Server;
let gatewayPort = 0;
let currentBlob: Record<string, unknown> = {};

beforeAll(async () => {
  originate = http.createServer((req, res) => {
    res.setHeader('Content-Type', 'application/json');
    if (req.url !== '/api/documents/' + DOC_ID) {
      res.writeHead(404);
      res.end('{}');
      return;
    }
    res.writeHead(200);
    res.end(JSON.stringify({ id: DOC_ID, status: 'anchored', contentHash: CONTENT_HASH, owner: { id: 'org-1' }, blockchain: currentBlob }));
  });
  originate.listen(0, '127.0.0.1');
  await new Promise<void>((r) => originate.once('listening', () => r()));
  const originateUrl = 'http://127.0.0.1:' + (originate.address() as AddressInfo).port;
  globalThis.fetch = (() => ({ ok: false, status: 404, json: async () => ({}), text: async () => '' })) as never;
  const { createVerificationRoutes } = await import('../routes/verification');
  const mockBodyParser: RequestHandler = express.json({ limit: '1mb' });
  const app = express();
  app.use(
    createVerificationRoutes({
      authenticateToken: () => (req, _res, next) => {
        (req as { user?: unknown }).user = { userId: 'u1', email: 'u@secuura.local', role: 'ADMIN', organizationId: 'org-1', tenantId: 't1', verificationLevel: 'FULL' };
        next();
      },
      mockBodyParser,
      query: vi.fn(async () => ({ rows: [] })) as never,
      isDbAvailable: () => false,
      redisService: {
        getPendingDocument: vi.fn(async () => null),
        getAllDocumentTypes: vi.fn(async () => []),
        getAllWorkflowInstances: vi.fn(async () => []),
        getNotificationSettings: vi.fn(async () => ({})),
        getRejectedDocument: vi.fn(async () => null),
        getWorkflowDocumentMapping: vi.fn(async () => null),
        getWorkflowInstance: vi.fn(async () => null),
      } as never,
      services: { originate: { url: originateUrl }, anchoring: { url: originateUrl } } as never,
      log: () => undefined,
      memWorkflowToDocumentMap: new Map(),
      memRejectedDocuments: new Map(),
      dbSaveRejection: vi.fn(async () => undefined),
      ADMIN_ROLES: ['ADMIN', 'admin'],
      enforceDocumentTypeRules: vi.fn(async () => ({ ok: true, docType: {} })) as never,
      createWorkflowInstanceIfRequired: vi.fn(async () => ({ gated: false })) as never,
      meetsVerificationLevel: () => true,
    }),
  );
  gateway = app.listen(0, '127.0.0.1');
  await new Promise<void>((r) => gateway.once('listening', () => r()));
  gatewayPort = (gateway.address() as AddressInfo).port;
});

afterAll(async () => {
  globalThis.fetch = realFetch;
  await new Promise<void>((r) => gateway.close(() => r()));
  await new Promise<void>((r) => originate.close(() => r()));
});

// drive the tier-1 verify route for one blob and answer verified and confidence
async function verify(blob: Record<string, unknown>): Promise<unknown[]> {
  currentBlob = blob;
  const url = 'http://127.0.0.1:' + gatewayPort + '/api/documents/' + DOC_ID + '/verify';
  const r = await realFetch(url, { method: 'POST', headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', Authorization: 'Bearer t' }, body: JSON.stringify({ purpose: 'test' }) });
  const body: any = await r.json();
  return [r.status, body.verified, body.verificationConfidence];
}

describe('KS-1123 F-1002-1 - a 0 or false anchor status stays off-chain-only on tier 1', () => {
  it('KS-1123 R1 - a status of 0 with a real hash and height is off-chain-only', async () => {
    CELLS_RUN += 1;
    expect(await verify({ txHash: REAL_TX, blockHeight: 4242, status: 0 })).toEqual([200, false, 'off-chain-only']);
  });
  it('KS-1123 R2 - a status of false with a real hash and height is off-chain-only', async () => {
    CELLS_RUN += 1;
    expect(await verify({ txHash: REAL_TX, blockHeight: 4242, status: false })).toEqual([200, false, 'off-chain-only']);
  });
  it('KS-1123 CONTROL - confirmed is on-chain and an empty-string status is off-chain-only', async () => {
    CELLS_RUN += 1;
    const confirmed = await verify({ txHash: REAL_TX, blockHeight: 4242, status: 'confirmed' });
    const empty = await verify({ txHash: REAL_TX, blockHeight: 4242, status: '' });
    expect([confirmed, empty]).toEqual([[200, true, 'on-chain'], [200, false, 'off-chain-only']]);
  });
  it('KS-1123 COMPLETENESS - every graded cell above actually ran', () => {
    expect(CELLS_RUN).toBe(EXPECTED_CELLS);
  });
});
```

Why each cell is what it is:
- **R1 (red):** a `0` status with a 64-hex hash and height 4242. At the untouched tip it passes. Under the tamper the read turns
  `0` into `null`, the tier-1 carve-out fires, and the cell FAILS by assertion:
  `expected [ 200, true, 'on-chain' ] to deeply equal [ 200, false, 'off-chain-only' ]`.
- **R2 (red):** the same with a `false` status; the same assertion red under the tamper.
- **CONTROL (green before and after):** a `'confirmed'` blob answers `200, true, 'on-chain'` (the harness CAN produce an on-chain
  answer, so the reds are not vacuous) and an empty-string status still answers `200, false, 'off-chain-only'` (the tamper keeps
  strings, so this row stays green under it).
- **COMPLETENESS:** asserts `CELLS_RUN === EXPECTED_CELLS` (3), so a file that summarises instead of transcribing cannot pass.

### READ THIS BEFORE YOU WRITE THE FILE

- The file you write is **exactly 113 lines**. If your output has fewer than 110 lines you have dropped something.
- Write every line of the fenced block above, verbatim, from the opening `/**` to the final `});`.
- Do **NOT** write "rest of the file unchanged", "// remaining tests omitted", `...` as a placeholder, or any other placeholder.
- All four `it(` blocks must be present, in order: `R1`, `R2`, `CONTROL`, `COMPLETENESS`. Three of them contain the line
  `CELLS_RUN += 1;`.

## Red cells

- KS-1123 R1 - a status of 0 with a real hash and height is off-chain-only
- KS-1123 R2 - a status of false with a real hash and height is off-chain-only

## Tamper (test-only mode - the checker plants this in a clone to prove your cells can go red)

line: 624
from: `    const persistedStatus = (doc as any).blockchain?.status ?? null;`
to: `    const persistedStatus = typeof (doc as any).blockchain?.status === 'string' ? (doc as any).blockchain.status : null; // TAMPER: KS-1123 red-proof, 0 and false read as statusless`

## Output

Exactly ONE ```diff block containing ONLY the new test file: `--- /dev/null` with NO leading space, then
`+++ b/Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/src/__tests__/ks1123-api-gateway-verify-an-empty-string.test.ts`, then
`@@ -0,0 +1,113 @@`, then the 113 lines above, each prefixed with `+`. Blank lines are a bare `+`. No hunk for `verification.ts` or
any other file.

## Premises (measured)

All times AEST 2026-09-17, each read from `date` in the run that produced it. Scratch clone = `git clone --shared --no-checkout` of the
Secuura checkout into `/private/tmp/claude-501/night/s17l/clone` (script `setup.sh`, 16:22:01-16:22:08, detached at `d7e95cd9f`),
moved to `f8c7aaa39` by `checkout_new.sh` (16:30:36) when origin develop moved, farmed and shared-built by
`tasks/code_patch/prepare_clone.sh` (rc 0 both times, source tracked-modified 0). Scripts in `s17l/k1123/`: `pre.sh` (one variant of
`verification.ts` from the pristine copy `verification.tip.ts`, line-keyed with the `from` text asserted, the test placed, `vitest run
--root` on that file or the whole suite, project tsc, restore with `cmp` rc 0, the test moved to `quarantine/`), `variant.py`,
`mkouts.py`, `runck.sh`, `clean.sh`, `assemble.py`. **Every vitest, tsc and checker run was under `sandbox-exec` with off-host
outbound denied (loopback allowed).** Nothing was deleted.

- **P1 tip.** origin develop = `d7e95cd9f153e9036ed77935a73c93504fa6e3dc` at 16:22:08, then `f8c7aaa39dabfe6a3916e5be55d9ccd752e7d8ed` at 16:29:56 (`git ls-remote` of the source's origin URL from the scratch clone with the source's `core.sshCommand`). The move is #1020 (KS-769) and touches ONE file, `scripts/audit/lock-discovery.mjs` (`git diff --name-only`). `routes/verification.ts` is blob `28fb58343` and the reference test blob `8c413fba6` at BOTH tips (`git rev-parse <tip>:<path>`); `verification.ts` last changed at `fa887f382` (KS-1176). Every checker run below ran at `f8c7aaa39`.
